              "id": "P53937",
              "source": "UniProtKB"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Component of the mitochondrial ribosome (mitoribosome), a dedicated translation machinery responsible for the synthesis of mitochondrial genome-encoded proteins, including at least some of the essential transmembrane subunits of the mitochondrial respiratory chain. The mitoribosomes are attached to the mitochondrial inner membrane and translation products are cotranslationally integrated into the membrane"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "commentType": "SUBUNIT",
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
              "id": "P53937",
              "source": "UniProtKB"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Component of the mitochondrial small ribosomal subunit (mt-SSU). Mature yeast 74S mitochondrial ribosomes consist of a small (37S) and a large (54S) subunit. The 37S small subunit contains a 15S ribosomal RNA (15S mt-rRNA) and at least 32 different proteins. The 54S large subunit contains a 21S rRNA (21S mt-rRNA) and at least 45 different proteins"
        }
      ]
    },
